Answers, in order:

1. Card.draft: no draft field, no transactions, no replica set. Generate and validate all 110 cards in memory, then one insertMany. If it throws, deleteMany({gameId}) (safe, because generation only runs in `setup`). Mongo stays a plain single node in compose.

2. Draw dedup: use your isActive idea, not a null filter. Add `isActive: boolean` (true on insert, false on undo), unique index on (gameId, number) with partialFilterExpression {isActive: true}. Keep undoneAt as the audit timestamp. Write a test proving a duplicate active insert fails and a re-insert after undo succeeds.

3. Game flags: yes, add showExactRankToPlayers (false), closeThreshold (3), maxOverlap (null), defaultCountryCode ("91"), appUrl, whatsappTemplate.

4. Inactive players: your proposal is fine. Excluded from hotNumbers, closeToWin and winners, still listed with a rank. includeInactiveInRank defaults to true.

5. URLs: ObjectId in paths. Serial only for verify-claim and ?q= search.

6. WinEvent: your schema, plus `placing`, `resolvedAt`, and a fourth status `withdrawn` (the causing draw was undone before confirmation).

7. Reset: clear Draws and WinEvents, and clear startedAt/finishedAt. Status goes back to `ready`. Keep players, cards, PIN hashes and the audit log (add a reset entry). Don't touch the in-memory PIN window.

8. In-memory lockout and idempotency: fine for v1, single instance. Put it in the README.

Your three deviations are approved: Noto Sans + Noto Sans Malayalam, @napi-rs/canvas, argon2id with a bcryptjs fallback only if the native build fails (tell me if it does).

Go. Scaffold per 00 section 7 and show me `npm install`, `npm run dev` and `npm test` working before Phase 1.